{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_4241fbeac06d3e97c164183b8465546028cd82147fed26bbac5c926376569049"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributions are welcomed via issue discussion or pull request with developer details in the development docs, and new-editor integrations follow a UX-consistency checklist."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5c6b83246d050c5a920f328a5e560024391d0bf578276efe022c78151e4d191e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"ECA supports configuring multiple agents/subagents, each with different models, tools, and behaviors."},{"claim_ids":["clm_bcaa4dd7944a227363f2f5b75e98e84d92c9f50f8b84ff41ee7bdb5f209112e4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Editors spawn the server via `eca server` and communicate over stdin/stdout using a JSON-RPC protocol inspired by LSP, so any editor can integrate."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cc6f81e534358cc1add6c2cfaba0c304997b1d8654e23a187fac6f7e41eb3612"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The server is written in Clojure with a layered layout: handlers.clj receives all JSON-RPC requests, db.clj holds in-memory state, llm_api.clj is the LLM facade, and llm_providers/ holds vendor adapters."},{"claim_ids":["clm_dbf5003be61d4eb18234969493881dc5e366c687a57e421a870f21f14719789a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"ECA places a server between editors and LLMs to centralize tool-call management, multi-LLM interaction, telemetry, and a single configuration shared across editors."}],"claim_ids":["clm_4241fbeac06d3e97c164183b8465546028cd82147fed26bbac5c926376569049","clm_5c6b83246d050c5a920f328a5e560024391d0bf578276efe022c78151e4d191e","clm_bcaa4dd7944a227363f2f5b75e98e84d92c9f50f8b84ff41ee7bdb5f209112e4","clm_cc6f81e534358cc1add6c2cfaba0c304997b1d8654e23a187fac6f7e41eb3612","clm_dbf5003be61d4eb18234969493881dc5e366c687a57e421a870f21f14719789a"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:47:30Z","created_by_operation":"op_83736ac7b167414d88aa4f1f2c3981f7","id":"pg_07dfcd4b262550ae8df3412369f19ae0","maturity":"draft